WEBVTT

00:02:29.752 --> 00:02:33.171
The person doing the asking is part of the problem, too.

00:02:33.171 --> 00:02:36.217
That's called interviewer bias.

00:02:36.217 --> 00:02:38.177
Interviewer bias is all about the effect

00:02:38.177 --> 00:02:40.346
that the person asking the questions

00:02:40.346 --> 00:02:42.136
has on the sample.

00:02:42.136 --> 00:02:44.858
Humans generally don't like confrontation.

00:02:44.858 --> 00:02:48.306
People worry that their answers may make them look bad.

00:02:48.306 --> 00:02:50.123
Therefore, we find that people tend to give

00:02:50.123 --> 00:02:52.540
socially desirable responses,

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.103
not necessarily their honest opinions,

00:02:55.103 --> 00:02:56.901
because they don't want to come across

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:57.703
as heartless,

00:02:57.703 --> 00:02:58.305
racist,

00:02:58.305 --> 00:02:59.784
or bigoted.

00:02:59.784 --> 00:03:02.451
And the way we word our questions matters too.